01_problem_discovery.md
Problem Statement
Organizations lose millions of dollars annually because knowledge decays, employees leave, and AI systems provide answers without proof.

Core Problems
1. Knowledge Decay
Enterprise documentation becomes outdated rapidly. When documentation is stale, AI agents confidently propagate incorrect information at scale.

49% of information employees find is already obsolete

62% of customer service agents report their reference materials are out‑of‑date

Documentation "starts drifting from reality" as soon as processes change

Traditional wikis become "graveyards of half‑true pages nobody reads"

2. Organizational Memory Loss
When employees leave, vital expertise walks out the door.

42% of the skills needed for a role disappear when someone departs

Organizations lose a generation's worth of corporate memory every ~20 years due to turnover

Without systematic transfer, new hires must "figure it out" on their own for months

Undocumented process details are forgotten permanently

3. AI Trust Gap
Generative AI often hallucinates, and teams can't verify answers.

Only 46% of users trust AI outputs despite 66% using AI tools

95% of corporate generative AI pilots are failing to produce productivity uplifts

62% of companies cite knowledge governance as their top AI deployment challenge

AI tools trained on stale corporate data "become a liability at scale"

Hidden Costs
Cost Category	Annual Impact
Poor data quality	$12.9 million per company (Gartner)
Lost organizational knowledge	$31.5 billion for Fortune 500 (IDC)
1,000-employee company	~$2.4 million annual loss
Employees repeating work	6+ hours per week per employee
Customers abandoning brand	32% after one bad experience
Goal
Build a platform that:

Preserves organizational memory

Detects stale information automatically

Provides trusted, verifiable AI answers

Grounds every output in source evidence

